#+TITLE: sqz NEWS – history of user-visible changes
#+STARTUP: content hidestars

* Changes in 0.2.0
** New features
   - `dane-client`.  Enable this to get support for fetching
     certificates using DANE.
   - `signer::Signer`
   - `sign::Builder::add_signer`, and `sign::Builder::add_signers` now
     take a `Signer` instead of a `Cert`.  This can be used to set the
     signer's user ID subpacket.

** Notable fixes
   - Upgrade sequoia-openpgp to fix:

     CVE-2026-115841: Degenerate DSA keys are accepted on the Nettle
     and OpenSSL backends

     CVE-2026-115839: RSA public keys with exponent 1 are accepted on
     the Nettle and OpenSSL backends

     CVE-2026-115838: Ed25519 identity and other low-order public keys
     are accepted for signature verification

     CVE-2026-115837: Argon2 string-to-key parameters are not limited
     by StandardPolicy

     CVE-2026-115836: Tolerant ASCII armor parsing can select a
     different block than a strict parser

     CVE-2026-115835: ASCII armor parsing buffers a line without a
     length limit

     CVE-2026-115834: User IDs and notation data are displayed without
     escaping control characters

   - Upgrade openpgp-cert-d to fix:

     CVE-2026-121475: Following a symbolic-linked write lock file
     enables arbitrary file truncation

     CVE-2026-121476: Following symbolic links when updating
     certificates enables arbitrary file modification

     CVE-2026-121477: Following symbolic links when reading
     certificates enables information disclosure

   - Upgrade `sequoia-net`, which addresses:

     CVE-2026-121473: Unbounded download buffering enables denial of
     service via malicious HKP or WKD server

     CVE-2026-121474: Following symbolic links when writing to a WKD
     enables arbitrary file truncation

* Started the NEWS file.
